  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Ballari?", answer: "Since no school inside Ballari runs the IB, we start by asking which school your child boards at, which online curriculum they follow, or which board they are switching from, along with the subject, level and exam session. We shortlist tutors who have recently taught that exact course and settle on a slot that fits your family's evening or weekend routine, with a free trial class online before anything is decided." },
    { question: "Are there any schools inside Ballari that teach IB or IGCSE?", answer: "No, honestly, there is not one currently. Ballari's schools run on the Karnataka State Board or CBSE almost without exception. Families who want the IB or a Cambridge/Edexcel IGCSE either board a child at a school in Bengaluru, roughly 300 kilometres away, or choose an accredited online international school and keep the child living in Ballari full time." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Ballari?", answer: "No. A tutor arriving at a family's door is something this service runs only within Gurugram and a limited part of Delhi NCR, nowhere else in the country, Ballari included. What happens here instead is a full live class, one to one, over video with a shared screen, run by a tutor based anywhere in India. It is genuine private tuition taken from home, simply not delivered by someone walking through the front door." },
    { question: "Which schools near Ballari should I actually know about for IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Stonehill International School in Bengaluru runs the full IB continuum, PYP through CP, with both day and boarding places. The International School Bangalore and Canadian International School, Bengaluru both run the IB Diploma. All three sit roughly five hours from Ballari by road, which is why families choosing them are almost always looking at boarding rather than a daily commute." },
    { question: "What actually determines the cost of an IB or IGCSE tutor for a Ballari family?", answer: "The level, how uncommon the subject is among currently teaching tutors, how long each session runs, and how recently the tutor has taught that specific syllabus all shape the fee, and we state it clearly for your case before any trial. Because the format is online everywhere, a tutor's own location does not change the price at all." },
    { question: "Is there a genuinely free trial class before we commit to anything?", answer: "Yes, and it happens before any decision, not after. A suggested tutor runs one real class on a topic taken straight from your child's own syllabus, at no cost and with nothing owed afterward. Only once that is done does the tutor set out what the opening month would cover, and it is entirely your choice whether to proceed, ask for changes, or look elsewhere." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with an IB Internal Assessment for a Ballari student?", answer: "Guidance, yes; writing it, never. A tutor can help settle on a workable research question, explain what a grading criterion is actually looking for, sanity-check a data-collection plan, and give honest feedback on a draft. Putting the tutor's own words into a document the student submits crosses into an academic integrity breach that is refused outright, no exceptions." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects does IB Gram cover for Ballari-connected students?", answer: "Coverage spans the standard six subject groups, with both Maths routes, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management and English A drawing the most enquiries from Ballari families, alongside Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance for whatever subject a student has chosen to write on." },
    { question: "Do you tutor MYP and PYP students connected to Ballari, not just the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, the full continuum is covered. MYP support usually focuses on moving from description into genuine criterion-based analysis, particularly in the sciences, plus steady help with the Year 5 Personal Project. PYP-age children work on reading confidence, writing structure and early number sense, in short sessions that fit around a family's own schedule." },
    { question: "Does online tutoring actually work well for a city with no IB or IGCSE school at all?", answer: "It works especially well here, because Ballari has no local specialist for something like IB Chemistry HL or IGCSE Additional Mathematics to begin with. A shared screen, worked examples and a tutor talking a problem through step by step cover most of what an in-room lesson would offer, while opening the choice to specialists anywhere in India rather than a short local list." },
    { question: "How are tutors checked before being matched to a Ballari family?", answer: "Every tutor is checked on qualifications, how recently they have taught the exact subject and level in question, and how they handle guiding assessed coursework, all before a name is ever suggested to a family. Since Ballari itself has no local supply of such tutors, we deliberately favour recent, hands-on experience over a generalist profile, and the trial class is where a family confirms the fit for themselves." },
    { question: "When is the right time for a Ballari family to start IB or IGCSE tutoring?", answer: "Ideally at the very start of the course, Grade 9 for IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma, which leaves room to fix foundations before internal exams, coursework deadlines and predicted grades all land together. A family starting later, even in the final year or right after a boarding-school move, can still make real progress by focusing on the highest-value topics and past papers." },
    { question: "My child is switching from the Karnataka State Board or CBSE, often alongside a move to a Bengaluru school. Can a tutor help?", answer: "This comes up often from Ballari families and is close to routine for us. The gap is usually exam language rather than content, since a switching student typically knows the material already: understanding precisely what an instruction word like 'evaluate' or 'analyse' is asking for, plus new habits around Internal Assessment and coursework planning. Starting over the summer before the board switch and any boarding move both take effect gives the best chance to settle in properly." },
    { question: "Can sessions be arranged around hostel timings or a parent's plant shift schedule?", answer: "Yes, this is one of the more specific things we plan around for Ballari families, whether a child is boarding in Bengaluru or a parent works rotating shifts connected to the steel plant. Sessions are typically set for weekday evenings, weekends, or defined hostel-leave windows, with revision blocks built around exam-season leave and breaks such as Ugadi and Dasara rather than fighting a fixed routine." },
    { question: "What if we are not happy with the tutor matched to our child?", answer: "Say so plainly, and a different tutor is found. We check in with families every few weeks specifically to catch this early, and a mismatch is treated as something to fix immediately rather than something a child should simply tolerate. There is no long contract attached, so sessions can also be paused or stopped at any point without cost." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school in Bengaluru, VSK University, JSW, the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No, this is an independent tutoring service with no formal connection to any school in Bengaluru or Ballari, to Vijayanagara Sri Krishnadevaraya University, to JSW or any employer, or to the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel. Any school named on this page appears only to show where families actually study, and tutors work strictly to that school's own calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

